Overlay patch 0040: visionOS is Metal-only — no ENABLE_OPENGL (= reference
0023, path retarget only; VISION-PRO-LUS-PLAYBOOK Phase 01).
visionOS has neither desktop GL (glew) nor GLES frameworks, so LUS's
OpenGL comparator backend cannot compile there. Upstream already guards
the whole backend (gfx_opengl.cpp body and the Fast3dWindow
instantiation) behind ENABLE_OPENGL — this patch just stops defining it
when SOH_VISIONOS is set. The iOS build is unchanged. Audit 2026-07-22:
on our fork this hunk lands in the else() branch that a correctly-flipped
(0039) vision build never takes — the iOS branch never defines
ENABLE_OPENGL — so it is defensive depth for any scope that evaluates
un-flipped; kept for reference diff-parity, zero-risk on iOS.

--- a/libultraship/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/libultraship/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -203,7 +203,8 @@
     endif()
 else()
     target_compile_definitions(libultraship PRIVATE
-        ENABLE_OPENGL
+        # SOH_IOS (overlay 0040): no GL of any kind on visionOS — Metal only.
+        $<$<NOT:$<BOOL:${SOH_VISIONOS}>>:ENABLE_OPENGL>
         $<$<CONFIG:Debug>:_DEBUG>
         $<$<NOT:$<CONFIG:Debug>>:NDEBUG>
         SPDLOG_ACTIVE_LEVEL=${SPDLOG_MIN_CUTOFF}
